commands.long:
Points each channel at the release: --agent names the agent and, after @, its version (1.4.0) or release number;
without a version it is the agent's newest release that is not revoked. Without --agent each channel keeps its agent.
A revoked release is never deployed. It asks for confirmation; --yes skips it.

Creates a package in directory, which must be missing or empty, from the function or mcp template of the
@caplo/tools SDK, which is embedded in the CLI at build time. --type is required. The package is named after the
directory unless --name is given. Run npm install in it before testing it.
